# valgrind suppressions for scripts/leak-check.sh (#151). Each entry says why it is not a leak.

# The mount of the binary's FUSE session (55 bytes, once per process): `serve` in
# src/main.rs keeps it in a ManuallyDrop on purpose, because its drop would unmount by path,
# and the path may hold a newer sacdfs's mount by then (#51). Once per process, no growth.
{
   sacdfs-session-mount-kept-on-purpose
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:_ZN5fuser3mnt5Mount3new*
   ...
   fun:_ZN6sacdfs3run*
}
